    <origin>Created 2026-07-22 by orchestrator (task-032 Path-A re-scope). See notes/task-032-pushannotations-scope.md.</origin>

    <owner-decision-required>
      🔔 PRODUCT DECISION (root §6.5 / §11) — the owner MUST choose before this task executes:
      DocxAnnotationWriter also byte-authors the DEPLOYED FR-24 "push-annotations / push-to-Word" surface
      (server `ComposeService.PushAnnotationsAsync` + endpoint `POST /api/compose/document/{id}/push-annotations`
      + push-preview endpoint (9b, FR-28); client `useComposePushAnnotations` in `useComposeWordShuttle.ts`,
      exported from `index.ts`). It is TEXT-ANCHORED (`DocxAnnotation.TargetText`) — cannot route through the
      `(paraId,runIndex,offset)` engine without whole-doc text-search (forbidden by I-7). Choose:
      • Path B — RETIRE push-annotations entirely (remove endpoints 9/9b + PushAnnotationsAsync + client hook +
        Word-shuttle push leg + tests), then delete DocxAnnotationWriter cleanly. Removes a deployed capability.
      • Path C — MIGRATE push-annotations to the op-log contract (accepted-annotation UI carries op anchors;
        server routes through the engine). Preserves the capability; larger client-UX rewrite; may be multi-task.
      Until chosen, this task stays blocked and DocxAnnotationWriter remains (interim 2-byte-author state,
      documented §6.5 Path-A exception).
    </owner-decision-required>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close out the last text-search byte-author. After the SAVE path moved onto ComposeShadowPatchEngine (task
    032), `DocxAnnotationWriter` (+ `DocxAnnotation.TargetText` + `LocateTarget` whole-doc text-search — the 422
    root cause + the I-7 violation) survives ONLY because it byte-authors the deployed FR-24 push-annotations
